    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="15a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 15a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.10-2"/> hwa þæne friðleasan man healde oððe flyman<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.star3"/> feormie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.11-2"/>, bete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, swa hit ær lagu wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf hwá ðonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.2"/> friðleasan man healde oððe feormie, bete, swa hit lagu wǽs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwa þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.1"/> fryðleasan man healde oððe feormige, bete þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, swa hit ær lagu wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.10"/><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis hominem pro<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.11"/> culpa exiliatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.12"/> tenuerit aut pauerit, emendet hoc, sicut ante legitimum fuit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui expulsum pauerit aut detinuerit pacifice, quem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.12-2"/> Angli uocant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.13"/> friðleasne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.14"/> man, reddat regi, sicut lex est, plenam emendationem, et illi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.15"/> qui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.16"/> expulsum expulit despectum suum, si ita iustum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.oe.17"/> est.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="15a" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="319" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis exlegem seruauerit uel procurauerit, satisfaciat, ut supra dictum est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="15a" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="180" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hwá ðonne<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15a.robnote.fn.8"/> friðleasan man healde oððe feormie<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_15a.robnote.fn.9"/>, bete swa hit<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_15a.robnote.fn.10"/> lagu wǽs.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="260" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa þæne friðleasan man healde oððe flyman feormie, bete þæt, swa hit ær lagu wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="318" ed="#liebermann"/>Und wenn jemand den (nun einen <hi rend="italic">B A</hi>?) friedlosen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.de.1"/> Menschen [schützend] erhält oder (einen Verbannten <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) beherbergt, büsse er das, wie es bisher<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.de.2"/> Rechtsordnung war.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_15a.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone keeps the (then an, B A?) outlawed man [under protection] or harbours (an outlaw, G), let him pay compensation for it as was the law before.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="181" ed="#robertson"/>And therefore if anyone maintains or harbours an outlawed man<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_15a.robnote.n.1"/>, he shall make amends in accordance with the established law<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_15a.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And if then anyone maintains or harbours an outlawed man,<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_15a.whinote.n.8"/> he is to pay compensation for it as the law was before.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="261" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And accordingly, if anyone protects or shelters an outlaw, he shall be penalized according to the law.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="318"><ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Ew. 5, 2</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 15a: (II Ew 5:2)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘flyman’ is probably G's addition. Liebermann compares II Ew 5.2.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 319, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">flyman: omitted AB</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">ær: omitted B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">15<hi rend="italic">a fehlt KR</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">15a lacking in KR</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">proprii <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">proprii T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> exhil. <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from exhil. Dm</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif h. ðonne fryþl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif h. ðonne fryþl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.star3" n="***" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">wohl G’s Zusatz; fehlt übr.; vgl.</hi> 12†</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">probably G’s addition; lacking in the others; cf. 12†</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-mige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-mige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">318</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 8, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. above 8, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">auf Rasur H;</hi> quod <hi rend="italic">Lb; verb. aus</hi> quod <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">on an erasure H; quod Lb; corrected from quod Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dicunt <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dicunt Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lesne <hi rend="italic">Cb;</hi> fredleseman <hi rend="italic">Lb;</hi> <hi rend="spaced">frendlesmanne</hi> <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lesne Cb; fredleseman Lb; <hi rend="italic">frendlesmanne</hi> S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">expulsionem illi et qui <hi rend="italic">wiederholt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">expulsionem illi et qui repeated by Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">est i. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">est i. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> friedlos 1f. (über <hi rend="italic">frendles</hi> 1m). Das Kompositum <hi rend="italic">frið-leas</hi> ist zwar Agsächs. in Bestandteilen und Bildung, begegnet aber als Terminus nur hier und gilt daher Steenstrup als vielleicht unter Dänischem Einfluss entstanden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> friedlos 1f. (on <hi rend="italic">frendles</hi> 1m). The compound <hi rend="italic">frið-leas</hi> is, it is true, Anglo-Saxon in its elements and formation, but occurs as a technical term only here, and Steenstrup therefore regards it as having perhaps arisen under Danish influence</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht Zitat von 13, 2, wie Cons missversteht, sondern von ungeschriebener Denalagu (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 11l), deren Partikularrecht fortbesteht. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 17</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not a citation of 13, 2, as Cons misunderstands it, but of the unwritten Denalagu (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 11l), whose particular law continues in force. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 17</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_15a.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">204</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Neben Strafgeld für den König setzt Inst noch ‘Ungehorsam’ (<hi rend="italic">s. d</hi>. 26c; Schutz 4b), der dem verbannenden Gerichtsherrn zufliesst. Nach dessen Stande stuft sich ab die Strafe für Widersetzlichkeit gegen seinen Spruch II Cn 15, 2. Hn 35, 1 (= 87, 5); <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. 41, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Besides a fine for the king, Inst also sets ‘disobedience’ (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word 26c; Schutz 4b), which goes to the lord of jurisdiction who pronounced the banishment. The penalty for defiance of his sentence is graded according to his rank, II Cn 15, 2. Hn 35, 1 (= 87, 5); <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. 41, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_15a.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The term <hi rend="italic">friðleas</hi> does not occur elsewhere, see Toller, <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi> p. 268 <hi rend="italic">s.v.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_15a.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. II Edw. 5, 2.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_15a.robnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">180</biblScope></bibl><label>ðonne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þæne</hi> G.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_15a.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">180</biblScope></bibl><label>feormie</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">o. flyman f.</hi> G.</seg></note>
